PRIVACY POLICY FOR SONUS

Last Updated: October 2026

1. WHAT DATA WE COLLECT
Uncle Dunc built Sonus as a Peer-to-Peer (P2P) game. This game is designed from the ground up to respect your privacy. 
- We do not collect, store, or share any personal information.
- We do not track your location, device data, or gaming habits.
- There are no account registration systems, analytics tools, or databases hosted by us.

2. HOW NETWORK CONNECTIVITY WORKS
Because this game utilizes a peer-to-peer network architecture, game data (such as player positions and movements) is transmitted directly between players over the network. We do not host, monitor, or intercept this game traffic.

3. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES
This game utilizes Discord Rich Presence to display your active gameplay session on your Discord profile. This integration only transmits basic session status (like game duration) to your local desktop Discord application. We do not collect or store your Discord account details.

4. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updates will be posted directly within the game's distribution channels.

5. CONTACT US
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, you can reach out to us at: sonus.game1@gmail.com
